title: NetApp Filer: Snapvault/Snapmirror Lag-time
agents: netapp
catalog: hw/storagehw/netapp
license: GPLv2
distribution: check_mk
description:
 The check monitors the lag-time of snapvault volumes and the transfer state of
 the underlying SnapMirror relationship.
 You can configure levels at which age the check should report {WARN} and {CRIT}.
 Per default there are no levels for the lag-time.
 The transfer states "failed", "aborted" and "hard_aborted" are {CRIT} by default,
 "queued", "success" and "transferring" are {OK}.
 Transfer states not known to Checkmk are {UNKN}.
 If ONTAP reports the relationship as unhealthy, the check is {CRIT} by default
 and shows the reasons reported by ONTAP. Older ONTAP versions may not
 report the health.
 The levels, the mapping of the transfer states and the state for unhealthy
 relationships can be configured with the rule "NetApp SnapVault / SnapMirror".

discovery:
 One service is created for each SnapMirror relationship, also for
 relationships that have no lag-time yet.

